      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've been treating the top of the stack as a register pool, but really there also needs to be built-in 64-bit int and float virtual registers. RV64-IMDV for a good reference set. A stack pointer and program counter would be great too, but not absolutely necessary.\nOpen-source royalty free\nhttps://riscv.org/specifications/",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-12-21T00:14:18.949Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Basic arithmetic and logic ops that would be much closer to hardware than the levels of redirection currently required.\nInstead of \n`PUSH, arg1`\n`PUSH, arg2`\n`PUSH, output`\n`EXTERN, \"SystemSingle.__op_Multiplication__SystemSingle_SystemSingle__SystemSingle\"`\nThere could be this\n`FMUL output, arg1, arg2`\nRelated: https://feedback.vrchat.com/vrchat-udon-closed-alpha-feedback/p/assembler-request-allow-arbitrary-variables\nImmediate mode would also be nice to have\n`ADD output, arg1, #24`\n",
